- Update to version 26.04.5.1ubuntu:
  * gtk3/render-assets: Also render the fallback symbolic assets (LP: #2147544)
  * gtk3: Adjust fallback assets colors and avoid recoloring them (LP: #2147544)
  * gtk: Re-render the fallback png assets (LP: #2147544)
  * gtk: Sync with upstream changes
  * icons/symlinks: Symlink distributor-logo with start-here (LP: #2147664)
  * icons: Generate distributor-logo symlinks (LP: #2147664)
  * gtk: Uniform window and menus border radius with libadwaita / shell
    (LP: #2147928)
  * gtk3/apps/ding: Adjust borders and paddings to match gnome-shell
    (LP: #2147938)
  * gtk3/apps/ding: Adjust separator margins to match gnome-shell
  * gtk: Ignore a warning on installing gtk2 symlinks
  * icons: Replace duplicated icons with symlinks at install time (LP: #2018772)
  * icons: Use meson native installation of symlinks and check for them
    (LP: #2018772)
  * icons/symlinks: Remove more duplicates using symlink lists (excluding the
    unity ones not to create a package dependency on icon theme) (LP: #2018772)
  * icons/symlinks/fullcolor: Symlink other duplicated icons (LP: #2018772)
  * icons: Regenerate symlinks (LP: #2018772)
  * debian/rules: Check that installed files only include valid symlinks
    We use quite a bit of symlinks, so let's ensure that each one is self-
    contained in each package and may not be split between different debian
    binaries (Related to LP: #2018772)

- Update to version 26.04.4.1ubuntu:
  * Icon/resources: Add source file (LP: #2147030)
  * Icon/showtime: Added source file (LP: #2147030)
  * build: Release 26.04.4
  * icons/generate-symlinks: Do not try to use an undefined variable
  * icons/generate-symlinks: Error out on using unbound variables
  * icons/showtime: Use more upstream-inspired colors and style (LP: #2147030)
  * build: Drop unused meson codepaths
    We depend on newer meson now, so all such code is dead
  * ci/render-icons: Install ubuntu fonts in CI.
    We need these fonts to render various assets where text is used and not
    embedded into the SVGs themselves, so adjust CI job to ensure icons are
    properly rendered.
    An example of badly rendered icons are the disk ones, where strings such
    as "SSD" are not centered, as they are using a fallback font
  * d/copyright: Add copyright for the oklab scss tools
  * icons: Re-render rendered icons as per accent color updates

